FAQ = [
 ("What is the best bed rack for a 2022+ Nissan Frontier?",
  "For a rooftop tent, Yakima's OverHaul HD towers: height adjusts from 19 to 30 in, rated 500 lb on-road and 300 lb off-road, with a limited lifetime warranty. They clamp to the bed rails, so they work on either bed length, but they're a universal product. Confirm the Frontier, the Utili-track setup and the crossbar length in Yakima's fit lookup. The fixed 13 in OutPost HD has the same ratings for $799."),
 ("Do 2005–2021 Frontier bed racks fit the 2022 Frontier?",
  "Don't assume so. The 2022 truck kept a revised frame and the 5 ft bed name, but accessory makers that engineer each truck separately list different parts: Retrax, BAK and Tyger all sell separate tonneau covers for the old 4'11\" (58.6 in) bed and the new 5' (59.5 in) bed. Racks that clamp to the rails may tolerate that change, but any \"2005–2025\" listing should be confirmed with the seller."),
 ("What is Utili-track and does it affect a bed rack?",
  "Utili-track is Nissan's bed channel system. Nissan describes three available channels on the current Frontier, and some trims and packages include it with two adjustable cleats. The channels run along the bed rails where many clamp racks grip, so a rack must either use the track or clear it. Yakima says tracked beds need Track Kit 1 or 2. Ask the maker which kit matches Utili-track before ordering."),
 ("Can I use a tonneau cover and a bed rack on the Frontier?",
  "Yes, if you plan them together. The RetraxPRO XR and BAK MX4 TS for the 2022+ Frontier have T-slot rails that take crossbars. Yakima's HD towers need Tonneau Kit 1 for select covers, and the BackRack combo here includes its tonneau hardware kit. Many budget clamp racks don't mention covers at all, so ask the seller before buying both, and check that a closed cover still clears the rack's feet."),
 ("Which bed length does my Frontier have?",
  "Crew Cab trucks come with the 5 ft bed or the 6 ft long bed, and King Cab trucks have the 6 ft bed. Listings print the short bed as 5' (59.5–60 in) and the long bed as 6' or 6'1\" (72.25–73.3 in), depending on where the maker measures. Clamp towers adjust to either. Fixed-frame racks need the right version, so measure bulkhead to tailgate if unsure."),
 ("What load rating do I need for a rooftop tent on a Frontier?",
  "Use the moving rating, not the parked one. Yakima rates its HD towers at 500 lb on-road and 300 lb off-road. The Thule Xsporter Pro Low is rated 220 lb, which suits kayaks and bikes rather than a tent with people inside. Add the tent, bedding, gear and the rack itself, then check the result against both the rack rating and the payload on your door-jamb sticker."),
 ("How high should a bed rack sit on a PRO-4X with a tent?",
  "Mid-height near the roofline is the common choice. Yakima's OutPost HD is fixed at 13 in, and the OverHaul HD adjusts from 19 to 30 in, so it can sit at the roofline or above it for room underneath. Low racks like the Thule Xsporter Pro Low stay below the cab. At full height, check the view of the third brake light from behind the truck with the load on."),
 ("Is a BackRack a bed rack?",
  "It's a headache rack: a steel frame at the front of the bed that guards the rear window, carries lights and gives ladders a front support. RealTruck lists the Original frame at $239.99 in 12-gauge steel. It won't carry a tent. The combo here pairs frame 15034 with the 50500 tonneau hardware kit for the 2022–2025 Frontier, so it works with a cover."),
 ("Will a bed rack affect Frontier towing?",
  "Not the tow rating, which is 6,720 lb, rising to 7,150 lb from 2025 on properly equipped trucks. What a rack changes is payload: its own weight, plus the tent and gear, comes out of the same figure that covers passengers and the trailer's tongue weight. Yakima lists the OverHaul HD towers at 59.52 lb before crossbars, so add it all up before a loaded trip with a trailer."),
]

